  "configuration_id": "config_014",
  "reason": "The RNA encoder is clearly the most impactful design choice: switching from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (config_022→config_046, all else identical) yielded the largest single improvement in the study (+7.1% accuracy, 0.635→0.706). However, we have not yet tested the third available learned encoder, scgpt. Config_014 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is an exact single-variable swap against our current best (config_046), isolating the RNA encoder effect while holding image encoder, aggregation, fusion, and profile setting constant. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the superior learned representation and lets us redirect remaining budget to other dimensions (e.g., aggregation or image encoder). Under a limited budget, resolving uncertainty on the highest-leverage design axis with a clean controlled comparison is the most efficient use of the next experiment."
}

